  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Isiolo Community Based Green Energy Project (CB-GEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of a 4 year programme, this project aims to increase access to modern, affordable and sustainable energy services for rural and peri-urban communities in Kenya. To do this, CAFOD, the Diocese of Kitui, the Diocese of Isiolo and Dupoto-e-Maa will work in partnership with CAFOD and Solar Works East Africa Limited, a private sector solar energy technology company. 

This project will target 73,628 households through 22 schools and health centres and 16 rural community based groups in the districts of Garbatulla and Isiolo.

Energy provision for schools and health centres will be enhanced through the installation of solar photovoltaic, water heating, refrigeration and purification systems. As a result school performance will be improved, as will drug storage in the health centres. 

Income generation of women and youth groups will be facilitated through the provision of ICT centres using solar-based computers and other office equipment, and commercial kiosks, all owned and managed by selected and trained youth groups.

Management of natural resources will be improved through the installation of solar water pumping systems at existing water structures, support for solar lighting systems for schools and health centres; by the use of energy saving stoves; and through community awareness raising on environmental protection.

Local partners and community groups will be trained to implement, maintain and manage the energy systems and on the benefits of sustainable environmental management, facilitating technology transfer and replication of the systems within the target areas.</narrative>
  </description>
